{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CesX4vFhNHUdwWAt5DyZk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add error code for the invalid state transition:\n   - Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to the `ErrorCode` enum to represent attempting to confirm a shipment that is in an invalid state (CANCELLED)\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add the confirm endpoint:\n   - Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n     - Takes the shipmentId from the path parameter\n     - Retrieves the shipment from the repository using `findById()`\n     - Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` with 404 if not found\n     - Throws `ConflictException` with 409 and `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` if the shipment is CANCELLED\n     - Updates the shipment to CONFIRMED status if it's CREATED\n     - Does nothing (idempotent) if already CONFIRMED\n     - Saves and returns the shipment as a ResponseEntity with 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add comprehensive tests:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and returns the same state\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409 and proper error code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment with 404 and proper error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\nI considered adding a separate \"confirm\" service/use-case class, but rejected this because:\n- The shipment feature is currently simple enough that this would be over-engineering\n- The repository already has `findById()` and `save()` methods\n- The existing controllers directly perform the state transitions without separate service classes\n- The constraint says \"Do not modify files outside the shipment feature\" - a new service class would violate this principle\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED)**:\n   - Read: Shipment from repository by ID\n   - Write: Updated shipment with CONFIRMED status to repository\n   - Return: 200 OK with updated shipment\n   - Mechanism: `findById()` and `save()` methods on repository\n\n2. **Idempotent path (CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED)**:\n   - Read: Shipment from repository by ID\n   - Write: Same shipment to repository (no change)\n   - Return: 200 OK with shipment\n   - Mechanism: Same as happy path, no conditional logic needed\n\n3. **Conflict path (CANCELLED)**:\n   - Read: Shipment from repository by ID\n   - Write: None\n   - Return: 409 Conflict with error code SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n   - Mechanism: ConflictException thrown, caught by GlobalExceptionHandler\n\n4. **Not found path**:\n   - Read: None (shipment not in repository)\n   - Write: None\n   - Return: 404 Not Found with error code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n   - Mechanism: ResourceNotFoundException thrown, caught by GlobalExceptionHandler\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `confirms a CREATED shipment` - Verifies state transition works: POST /shipments/{id}/confirm returns 200 with status=CONFIRMED\n2. `confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds` - Verifies idempotency: POST twice returns 200 both times\n3. `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409` - Verifies conflict detection: POST /shipments/{id}/confirm on CANCELLED returns 409 with error code\n4. `reports unknown shipment through error envelope` - Verifies not found: POST /shipments/missing/confirm returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":822,"cache_read_input_tokens":17195,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":822},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3946d836-